For secure PHP coding, always validate and sanitize user inputs to prevent injection attacks. Use prepared statements for database interactions. To print output as HTML, use the `htmlspecialchars()` function to escape any special characters. Here's a sample code snippet:

```php
<?php
$userInput = $_GET['input'];
$safeInput = htmlspecialchars($userInput, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8');
echo "<p>User input: $safeInput</p>";
?>
```

This ensures that any HTML tags in the user input are escaped and displayed as plain text, enhancing security.
